1ikl|n|A feather. ; A wing. ; An instrument used for writing with ink, formerly made of a reed, or of the quill of a goose or other bird, but now also of other materials, as of steel, gold, etc. Also, originally, a stylus or other instrument for scratching or graving. ; Fig.: A writer, or his style; as, he has a sharp pen. ; The internal shell of a squid. ; A female swan. ; To shut up, as in a pen or cage; to confine in a small inclosure or narrow space; to coop up, or shut in; to inclose. ; A small inclosure; as, a pen for sheep or for pigs.	a:12of,75,1~12of,75,1	v:1n1q,15,2~1n1q,15,2	n:ttc,113,1;1n1q,35,8~1n1q,35,8;ttc,113,1	N:1kzo,93,1~1kzo,93,1
