1iw4|a|Brought to consummation or completeness; completed; not defective nor redundant; having all the properties or qualities requisite to its nature and kind; without flaw, fault, or blemish; without error; mature; whole; pure; sound; right; correct. ; Well informed; certain; sure. ; Hermaphrodite; having both stamens and pistils; -- said of flower. ; To make perfect; to finish or complete, so as to leave nothing wanting; to give to anything all that is requisite to its nature and kind.	j:d1x,55,4;d1u,55,6;1uo3,53,4;1v7h,52,33;1ucy,46,6;wa2,46,5;1ud1,45,3;24t,45,2;aex,44,12;1fgw,40,4;snh,39,11;hr2,37,1;2bcg,36,7;1xs2,29,10;138,28,5~1v7h,52,33;1n1i,9,18;qk7,24,15;aex,44,12;snh,39,11;1xs2,29,10;1n1v,24,10;2abm,10,10;6wp,4,9;1ov7,24,8;2bcg,36,7;16ho,6,6;1ucy,46,6;rch,20,6;d1u,55,6	e:1d7f,57,11;17fr,43,3;2d2,41,19;bb,32,3;6lt,29,5;1dkt,3,2~2d2,41,19;1d7f,57,11;6lt,29,5;bb,32,3;17fr,43,3;1dkt,3,2
